    "approved_definition_context": [
      "stdGaussian E is the centered identity-covariance Gaussian probability measure. Measure.map is pushforward; Measure.prod is independent product; Measure.infinitePi is the countable independent product law.",
      "volume is canonical Lebesgue measure. Ioc(a,b) means a<r<=b; Icc(a,b) means a<=r<=b. The real interval endpoint distinction is null for Lebesgue measure. poissonMeasure r is the Poisson probability law with nonnegative mean r.",
      "gradient f is the actual real inner-product gradient. Differentiable means differentiability everywhere. LipschitzWith beta is the global distance bound. NNReal denotes nonnegative real numbers.",
      "Integrable asserts Bochner integrability. ENNReal is the extended nonnegative reals; ENNReal.ofReal maps a real to its nonnegative part. The real integrals are signed Bochner integrals and the lintegrals are nonnegative integrals.",
      "Measure.tilted mu m is the exponential tilt with density ofReal(exp(m)/integral exp(m) dmu). rnDeriv is the actual Radon-Nikodym derivative, and AbsoluteContinuous denotes measure absolute continuity.",
      "Nat.find chooses the least natural number satisfying its supplied existence proof. A dependent if separates the existence and nonexistence cases. Fin n indexes exactly 0 through n-1; tsum is the displayed infinite sum. Natural numbers are cast to ENNReal where that type is expected.",
      "All local constants, including generated proof terms, have been expanded from the compiled theorem type and checked with Lean Meta.isDefEq. Let-bound values keep their displayed scopes; proof terms establish typing conditions rather than additional mathematical assumptions.",
      "Supplementary type-explicit anonymous acceptance definition, extracted from the same compiled local definition and definitionally checked. It is instantiated at B=1 in the statement. This disambiguates the product index omitted by notation in the main view:\nfun {X} {A} W B =>\n  @Set.ofPred (Prod X (Prod Nat (Prod (Nat → A) Real))) fun p =>\n    @LE.le Real Real.instLE\n      (@Prod.snd (Nat → A) Real (@Prod.snd Nat (Prod (Nat → A) Real) (@Prod.snd X (Prod Nat (Prod (Nat → A) Real)) p)))\n      (@Finset.prod (Fin (@Prod.fst Nat (Prod (Nat → A) Real) (@Prod.snd X (Prod Nat (Prod (Nat → A) Real)) p))) Real\n        Real.instCommMonoid\n        (@Finset.univ (Fin (@Prod.fst Nat (Prod (Nat → A) Real) (@Prod.snd X (Prod Nat (Prod (Nat → A) Real)) p)))\n          (Fin.fintype (@Prod.fst Nat (Prod (Nat → A) Real) (@Prod.snd X (Prod Nat (Prod (Nat → A) Real)) p))))\n        fun i =>\n        @HDiv.hDiv Real Real Real (@instHDiv Real (@DivInvMonoid.toDiv Real Real.instDivInvMonoid))\n          (@HAdd.hAdd Real Real Real (@instHAdd Real Real.instAdd) B\n            (W\n              (@Prod.mk X A (@Prod.fst X (Prod Nat (Prod (Nat → A) Real)) p)\n                (@Prod.fst (Nat → A) Real\n                  (@Prod.snd Nat (Prod (Nat → A) Real) (@Prod.snd X (Prod Nat (Prod (Nat → A) Real)) p))\n                  (@Fin.val (@Prod.fst Nat (Prod (Nat → A) Real) (@Prod.snd X (Prod Nat (Prod (Nat → A) Real)) p))\n                    i)))))\n          (@HMul.hMul Real Real Real (@instHMul Real Real.instMul)\n            (@OfNat.ofNat Real (nat_lit 2)\n              (@instOfNatAtLeastTwo Real (nat_lit 2) Real.instNatCast\n                (@Nat.instAtLeastTwoHAddOfNat (@OfNat.ofNat Nat (nat_lit 1) (instOfNatNat (nat_lit 1)))\n                  (@Nat.instNeZeroSucc (@OfNat.ofNat Nat (nat_lit 0) (instOfNatNat (nat_lit 0)))))))\n            B))"
    ]
